        <p style="margin-top:14px">Most dental plans follow a 100 / 80 / 50 structure, which means the plan pays a higher share for preventive care and a smaller share for major work.</p>
        <ul class="check-list">
          <li><strong>Preventive care.</strong> Cleanings, exams, and routine x-rays, often covered at 100 percent with no waiting period.</li>
          <li><strong>Basic care.</strong> Fillings, simple extractions, and some root canals, often covered around 80 percent.</li>
          <li><strong>Major care.</strong> Crowns, bridges, dentures, and oral surgery, often covered around 50 percent after a waiting period.</li>
          <li><strong>Orthodontics.</strong> Braces and aligners for kids and sometimes adults, available on plans that include an ortho benefit.</li>
        </ul>
